# The .ko-agent-sandbox/egress/allowed of a project that opts into npm's audit service.
# npm sends a package/version inventory to the public registry, which may include
# private-registry and git dependency names. The allowance also lets any sandbox process send
# any body to that fixed path; every other registry POST and every PUT stays refused.
# The response supplies install-time warnings; it does not fail npm install. Use an explicit
# `npm audit --audit-level=high` when findings should fail a job.
# Leaving this out blocks automatic inventory disclosure and the POST-body channel, not the
# lower-bandwidth channel in allowed GET URLs. SECURITY.md, "Exfiltration through an allowed host".
+host registry.npmjs.org allow=npm-audit
